-- Refs #182 (pool data inconsistencies, part 2 of 4: move mixed-map pool_gameobject members to the per-map pool)
-- ERROR CLASS: "`pool_gameobject` has gameobject spawns on multiple different maps for gameobject guid (G) in pool id (P), skipped."
--   3858 lines per boot (PoolMgr.cpp:614). Each skipped gameobject was never spawned (ObjectMgr.cpp:2492 skips pooled GOs).
-- ROWS: 1906 UPDATEs (one per pool+map), 3858 pool_gameobject rows moved from the old pool P to the new piece pool for the GO's own
--   map (gameobject.map). The rows that stay in P are those on the map of the pool's first loaded member (the core's current choice).
-- SOURCE OF TRUTH: gameobject.map of each guid (verified with the world DB; identical in the MoP 5.4.8 data). Needs _40 first.
-- Idempotent: each UPDATE is keyed on the exact guids AND the old pool_entry, so a second run matches 0 rows.
